    "title": "Rising creatinine on TDF in pregnancy",
    "message": "Guidelines require serum creatinine and eGFR monitoring for patients on TDF. Creatinine rose from 0.8 to 1.1 mg/dL and eGFR dropped to 78 mL/min/1.73m² within 10 weeks of starting TDF. TDF is a known cause of renal toxicity including chronic kidney disease and Fanconi syndrome. Pregnancy itself increases renal workload and may contribute. The urinalysis is normal with no protein or glucose, which argues against significant tubular damage. However, the upward creatinine trend warrants close surveillance. Phosphate is normal at 3.8 mg/dL, providing further reassurance against Fanconi syndrome.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Repeat creatinine and eGFR within 4 weeks. If creatinine continues to rise, consider switching TDF to TAF per pregnancy guidelines.",
